    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Charming 3-bed cottage on elevated site overlooking the waters leading out to Blacksod Bay, & within a 3 minute drive of Belmullet Town.\r\n\r\nSet in an elevated position along the spectacular Wild Atlantic Way, this charming three-bedroom cottage enjoys a wonderful setting in Carne, just outside Belmullet, with distant views towards the waters leading out to Blacksod Bay. \r\n\r\nThe accommodation is well laid out and comprises a welcoming front porch, entrance hallway, living room, kitchen/dining room, utility room, WC, inner halls and three bedrooms. The property also benefits from a large, detached shed, providing excellent additional storage and offering considerable versatility for those requiring space for hobbies, equipment, recreational gear or general storage.\r\n\r\nA particular attraction of the location is its immediate proximity to Carne Golf Links, situated just behind the property. Widely regarded as one of Ireland's outstanding natural links courses, Carne is a dramatic 27-hole links course set amongst magnificent Atlantic sand dunes, making this an especially appealing location for golf enthusiasts.\r\n\r\nBeyond the golf course lies an extraordinary coastal landscape waiting to be explored. The surrounding Mullet Peninsula and Erris offer an exceptional quality of life for anyone drawn to the sea, walking, wildlife, surfing, fishing and outdoor pursuits. The coastline is dotted with beautiful sandy beaches, dramatic cliffs and sweeping Atlantic views, providing endless opportunities to explore and enjoy the great outdoors.\r\n\r\nThe Erris Head Loop, Cross Loops and numerous other local walking routes provide the opportunity to experience the remarkable scenery of the peninsula on foot, with breathtaking views across the Atlantic Ocean, surrounding bays and rugged coastline.\r\n\r\nThe area is also steeped in natural and cultural heritage. Blacksod Bay, Blacksod Lighthouse, Ballyglass Lighthouse, Eagle Island, Annagh Head, Benwee Head and the Inishkea Islands are all within the wider area and provide wonderful destinations for days out and exploration.\r\n\r\nThe vibrant town of Belmullet is approximately a three-minute drive away, providing an excellent range of day-to-day amenities including primary and secondary schools, shops, cafés, restaurants, pubs, hotels, church services, and even a natural tidal pool.\r\n\r\nThe larger towns of Ballina, Castlebar and Westport are also within easy reach, approximately an hour's drive away, providing access to a broader range of employment opportunities, shopping, healthcare, and leisure facilities.\r\n\r\nThis is a wonderful opportunity to acquire a charming home in a beautiful coastal setting. With Carne Golf Links on the doorstep, spectacular beaches, walking trails, and Belmullet town just minutes away, this property offers an enviable combination of tranquility, convenience and lifestyle."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Front Porch 1.29m (4'3\") x 1.8m (5'11\")\r\nWith a carpet floor.\r\n\r\nEntrance Hallway 3.75m (12'4\") x 0.97m (3'2\")\r\nWith a carpet floor and coving to the ceiling.\r\n\r\nLiving Room 3.56m (11'8\") x 3.96m (13'0\")\r\nBright room to the front of the property with a carpet floor, coving to the ceiling, and inset stove. A large window provides ample natural light.\r\n\r\nHall 3.02m (9'11\") x 0.92m (3'0\")\r\n\r\nHall 2.84m (9'4\") x 0.99m (3'3\")\r\n\r\nKitchen 3.06m (10'0\") x 4.57m (15'0\")\r\nSpacious room with lino flooring, fitted kitchen with tiled splashback, and a solid fuel stove. Two windows provide natural light and countryside views.\r\n\r\nUtility Room 3.04m (10'0\") x 3.01m (9'11\")\r\nBright room with a concrete floor and a large window providing natural light.\r\n\r\nWC 1.89m (6'2\") x 2.46m (8'1\")\r\nFully tiled with a toilet, pedestal sink, and shower. A window provides natural light and ventilation.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 4.08m (13'5\") x 4.07m (13'4\")\r\nDouble room with timber flooring, coving to the ceiling, and a large window providing natural light.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 4.08m (13'5\") x 3.07m (10'1\")\r\nDouble room with timber flooring, coving to the ceiling, and a large window providing natural light.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 3.08m (10'1\") x 4.01m (13'2\")\r\nDouble room with timber flooring and a large window providing natural light."
